fix(bot): show alerts as text, not as HTML source

Telegram's answerCallbackQuery does not parse HTML, so an alert built from a
screen's copy showed the tags themselves — <b>این دکمه دیگر معتبر نیست</b> — and
with premium emoji configured, a raw <tg-emoji> element.  app.bot.utils gains
alert_text(), which strips the markup, keeps the Unicode emoji, collapses the
line breaks and trims to the alert limit; every handler that answers a callback
with a message body now goes through it, and answer_callback() does it for
alert=True on its own.

The keys that reach an alert are checked for markup in tests/test_alert_text.py,
and the dispatcher-level test asserts the alert a customer actually receives is
tag-free and placeholder-free.
